      "content": "Semiconductor growth decelerated to 4.2% from 6.8% in Q2, yet AI chips surged 15.5% YoY, while automotive EV demand dropped 2.1% against a $12.4 billion niche revenue. Consumer electronics saw smartphone shipments decline 3.4%, contrasting with a 0.8% rise in wearables, as green tech infrastructure investment climbed 12%. Manufacturing costs rose 1.5%, counteracted by 2.2% efficiency gains, with the total volatility index settling at 18.4 from 22.1.",
      "source": "target",
